==Icelandic==

===Etymology===
From {{term|leggja á||to put on|lang=is}}, from {{term|leggja||to put, to lay|lang=is}} and {{term|á||on|lang=is}} and {{term|minnið||the memory|lang=is}} the definite article accusative singular of {{term|minni||memory|lang=is}}.

===Noun===
{{is-verb-weak|lagði|lagt|11=á minnið}}

# {{context|transitive|governs the accusative}} to [[keep]] in [[mind]], to [[memorise]], to [[study]], to [[learn]]
#: ''Allir þurfa að '''leggja''' reglurnar '''á minnið'''.''
#:: Everybody needs to '''memorise''' the rules.

====Usage notes====
* The thing or object which is being ''memorised'' or ''kept in mind'' is used between {{term|leggja|lang=is}} and {{term||á minnið|on memory}} in the accusative form:
*: ''Við þurfum að '''leggja''' alla bókina '''á minnið''' fyrir prófið!''
*:: We need to '''memorise''' the whole book for the test.

